# xargs(1)

## NAME

xargs - build and run commands from standard input

## SYNOPSIS

    xargs [-0rt] [-n max-args] [-I replace] [command [arg...]]

## DESCRIPTION

Reads words from standard input and runs the command (default `echo`) with them added as arguments. Words are separated by blanks and newlines; quotes and `\` can be used.

## OPTIONS

- `-0`: words are separated by NUL
- `-n N`: at most N words per command
- `-I replace`: run once per line, replacing the string in the arguments
- `-r`: do not run the command when there are no words
- `-t`: print each command before running it

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `123`: a command exited with 1 to 125
- `124`: a command exited with 255
- `125`: a command was killed by a signal
- `126`: the command could not be started
- `127`: the command was not found

